{
    "background_story": "Eric was a philosophy professor with a passion for the works of S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard. He spent most of his days pouring over the Danish philosopher's writings, trying to make sense of the complexities of human existence. As he delved deeper into Kierkegaard's ideas on the individual's subjective experience and the leap of faith, Eric found himself questioning his own life choices. He began to see the world as a place of inherent uncertainty, where true meaning could only be found through individual commitment and risk. Eric's newfound understanding of Kierkegaard's philosophy inspired him to take a leap of his own, leaving behind the security of academia to pursue a life of writing and art. Though the path ahead was uncertain, Eric felt a sense of liberation and purpose, knowing that he was embracing the existential freedom that Kierkegaard had written about so eloquently.",
